DeskWall is an independent project inspired by Deskland Preview
(https://github.com/BLEZZ0102/Deskland, GPL-3.0, Copyright (C) 2026 Deskland authors).
The original Deskland source was imported as this repository's first commit and is kept in
git history.

The "Beach" and "Meadow" themes in apps/desktop/public/themes/classic/ (page code, scripts,
sprite images and thumbnails) are ported from Deskland Preview's prototype/ folder under
GPL-3.0, with the changes listed in tools/vendor_classic_themes.py. The DeskWall code (Rust/Tauri host, three.js scene, settings app) is a new
implementation; the desktop-attachment approach in apps/desktop/src-tauri/src/desktop/windows.rs
follows the technique documented in Deskland's host. DeskWall is not affiliated with or
endorsed by the Deskland authors, and does not use the Deskland name, logo or icon as its own.

The "Autumn Forest" theme (apps/desktop/public/themes/classic/forest.*) is DeskWall's own work;
its icon field and hosting protocol follow the ported Meadow page. Animals, falling leaves and
small ground details are painted procedurally at startup. The tree crowns
(assets/forest-crowns.webp, forest-shadows.webp) are rendered with tools/forest/render_trees.py
from Quaternius' "Stylized Nature MegaKit" (CC0, https://quaternius.com), and the forest floor
(assets/forest-ground.webp) is derived from Poly Haven's "Leaves Forest Ground" (CC0,
https://polyhaven.com/a/leaves_forest_ground).

Third-party dependencies keep their own licenses (see each package's metadata).
